# Typing that starts the instant a format switch is asked for, with no pause for the switch to
# settle. During the switch the keyboard passes from one editor to the other; nothing typed in
# that moment may be lost. A slow or busy machine (a screen reader makes it more so) stretches
# the moment, which is how typed text went missing.

== Typing straight after switching to HTML
modes: plain
keys: ^+3
type: alpha beta gamma
wait: 2
mode-is: html
text-is: alpha beta gamma

== Typing straight after switching to Markdown
modes: plain
keys: ^+2
type: alpha beta gamma
wait: 2
mode-is: markdown
text-is: alpha beta gamma

== Typing straight after switching from HTML to Plain Text
modes: html
keys: ^+1
type: alpha beta gamma
wait: 2
mode-is: plain
text-is: alpha beta gamma

== Typing straight after switching from HTML to Markdown
modes: html
keys: ^+2
type: alpha beta gamma
wait: 2
mode-is: markdown
text-is: alpha beta gamma

== Typing straight after switching from Markdown to HTML
modes: markdown
keys: ^+3
type: alpha beta gamma
wait: 2
mode-is: html
text-is: alpha beta gamma

== Bold, then typing, straight after switching to HTML
modes: plain
keys: ^+3
keys: ^b
type: alpha beta
keys: ^b
wait: 2
text-is: alpha beta
markdown-is: **alpha beta**

== Typing straight after the format question is answered Yes
judgment: After a format switch the caret is at the top of the body, so what is typed next goes in front of the text. Should the caret keep its place (or go to the end) across a switch?
modes: html
keys: ^b
type: bold
keys: ^b
keys: ^+1
wait: 1.5
front-is: Switch to Plain Text
keys: y
type: "after "
wait: 2
mode-is: plain
text-is: after bold

== Typing straight after the format question is answered No
modes: html
keys: ^b
type: bold
keys: ^b
keys: ^+1
wait: 1.5
front-is: Switch to Plain Text
keys: n
type: " after"
wait: 2
mode-is: html
text-is: bold after

== Typing straight after Alt+Y from Subject
text: body
keys: %u
wait: 0.5
keys: %y
type: " more"
wait: 1.5
text-is: body more

== Typing straight after the context menu is closed
text: body
keys: +{F10}
wait: 1
keys: {ESC}
type: " more"
wait: 1.5
text-is: body more

== Typing straight after coming back from another window
text: body
window: main
wait: 1.5
window: message
type: " more"
wait: 1.5
text-is: body more
